-- title:
--   Existence and uniqueness of the local fundamental class
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a finite extension $L$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q`, together with a finite group $G$ acting faithfully on $L$ by semiring automorphisms and acting multiplicatively on $L^\times$, the two actions being compatible ($(g\cdot u)$ and $g\cdot u$ agree in $L$ for units $u$) and the action fixing the image of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in $L$ pointwise; assume $G$ is solvable. Let $K$ be a further finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ inside `PadicAlgCl q` which is a base for $(L,G)$, i.e. $K \le L$ and an element of $L$ lies in $K$ exactly when it is fixed by all of $G$. The conclusion is that there is exactly one class $u \in H^2(G, L^\times)$, with $L^\times$ regarded additively as a $\mathbb{Z}$-representation of $G$, which is a local fundamental class in the sense of `IsLocalFundamentalClass`: for every finite extension $M \supseteq L$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$ in `PadicAlgCl q`, every finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$ and on $M^\times$, normal subgroups $N_L, N_n \le H$, isomorphism $e : G \simeq H/N_L$, element $\varphi \in H$ and unit $\pi \in M^\times$ forming an unramified over-layer datum (the $H$-action fixes $\mathbb{Q}_q$ and is compatible with the action on units, $K$ is the $H$-fixed part and $L$ the $N_L$-fixed part of $M$, the $G$-action on $L$ matches the $H$-action through $e$, $\#(H/N_n) = \#G$, $H/N_n$ is generated by the image of $\varphi$, $\varphi$ acts on $N_n$-invariant elements of norm $\le 1$ as the Frobenius raising to the power $\#$ of the residue field of `Rw q K`, and $\pi$ is $H$-fixed, lies in $K$, has norm $<1$ and has maximal norm among $N_n$-invariant elements of norm $<1$), and every morphism $\iota$ from the restriction of $L^\times$ along $H \to H/N_L \simeq G$ to $M^\times$ which is the identity on underlying elements, the image of $u$ under the degree-$2$ map induced by $(H \to H/N_L \simeq G, \iota)$ equals the inflation from $H/N_n$ of the class of the carry cocycle `carryFun` for the generator $\varphi N_n$ with value $\pi$, namely the cocycle sending a pair whose cyclic logarithms sum to at least the order of $\varphi N_n$ to $\pi$ and all other pairs to $1$.
--
--   This is the existence and uniqueness of the local fundamental class $u_{L/K} \in H^2(\mathrm{Gal}(L/K), L^\times)$ for a solvable layer of $q$-adic fields, normalised by its prescribed values on unramified cyclic over-layers with a given uniformiser. It is the input to the local components of the idelic Artin map and of the Herbrand-type computations built on them.
